  <h2 id="revision">One-minute revision</h2>
  <Callout kind="revision">
    <ul>
      <li>Scale because of distances (kNN, k-means, SVM, PCA), gradient descent conditioning (linear/logistic, nets) and fair weight penalties. Trees do not care.</li>
      <li>Standardize <Math tex="(x-\mu)/\sigma" /> by default; min-max for bounded, outlier-free data; robust (median, IQR) for heavy tails; <Math tex="\log(1+x)" /> for positive skew.</li>
      <li>Fit on train only; transform val, test and production with frozen statistics. Pipeline + ColumnTransformer. Fitting before splitting is leakage.</li>
      <li>Nominal → one-hot (drop one with an intercept: dummy trap; <code>handle_unknown</code> for new values). Ordinal → ordered integers. Never integer-code nominal data for linear models.</li>
      <li>Many categories: out-of-fold smoothed target encoding (leakage risk), hashing, or embeddings (= one-hot + weight matrix).</li>
      <li>Cyclic features: sin and cos. Binary: one 0/1 column.</li>
      <li>Skewed positive target: model <Math tex="\log y" />, invert for reporting. Missing values: impute with training statistics, add an indicator; boosted trees handle NaN natively.</li>
      <li>Later: tokens are a 50k-way categorical and the embedding table is their learned encoding; LayerNorm (week 6) is scaling inside the network.</li>
    </ul>
  </Callout>
